From dcb11138d50a304a35200e4097ca707fa59cb5d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:33:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 077/144] drm/msm/dp: keep HPD initialization after connector
 detection

Connector detection may set plugged before the initial HPD event. The
multiple-plug reference guard must not skip AUX/PHY setup, panel capability
discovery or EDID acquisition in that case: get_modes expects HPD to have
populated the EDID already.

Take a connection runtime-PM reference only when the connection was not
already detected, while retaining the existing HPD initialization path for
both first and repeated events. Connector detection separately owns its
temporary scoped reference and the single connection-state reference.

This adapts the multiple-plug guard to the existing detect/HPD ordering;
connection teardown and the remaining HPD event series are unchanged.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024-hpd-irq-events-v8-6-6ee949e7a384@oss.qualcomm.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024051952.2006-1-26rote@gmail.com/

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0099-drm-msm-dp-keep-HPD-initialization-after-connector-d.patch
Import-SHA256: b2438e260c7eab204cd498cf4e028e8ea82c5220837062a567ed6f5f20aa7fc8
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit a6a9d51dd6186984d6d5fd8d65c96d7d61195a1e)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 13 ++++++-------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 4af6f57f26..1c1160e36c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -411,13 +411,12 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
 
-	if (dp->plugged)
-		return 0;
-
-	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
-	if (ret) {
-		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
-		return ret;
+	if (!dp->plugged) {
+		ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
+		if (ret) {
+			DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
+			return ret;
+		}
 	}
 
 	msm_dp_aux_enable_xfers(dp->aux, true);
